<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<meta name="generator" content="qpcr-assay-check {{ r.tool.version }}">
<title>{{ assay.assay_name }} – assay evaluation record ({{ status_label }})</title>
<style>
:root {
  --ink: #17222D; --muted: #55636F; --paper: #F4F6F8; --panel: #FFFFFF; --rule: #D3DBE2;
  --pass: #1F7A5A; --pass-bg: #DDF0E7;
  --warn: #9A5F00; --warn-bg: #FBEBC8;
  --fail: #B23B3B; --fail-bg: #F6D9D9;
  --incomplete: #46566B; --incomplete-bg: #DCE2EA;
  --info: #55636F; --info-bg: #E6EAEE;
  --serif: "Iowan Old Style", "Palatino Linotype", Palatino, Georgia, serif;
  --sans: system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif;
  --mono: ui-monospace, "SF Mono", Menlo, Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace;
}
* { box-sizing: border-box; }
html { background: var(--paper); }
body { margin: 0; color: var(--ink); font-family: var(--serif); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.55; }
main { max-width: 96rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
h1, h2, h3, table, .chip, .meta, .rec { font-family: var(--sans); }
h1 { font-size: 1.9rem; line-height: 1.2; margin: 0 0 .35rem; }
h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 3rem 0 .75rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }
h3 { font-size: 1rem; margin: 1.75rem 0 .5rem; }
p { margin: .6rem 0; max-width: 46rem; }
.meta { color: var(--muted); font-size: .85rem; }
.meta code { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .8rem; word-break: break-all; }


table.summary th[scope=row] { min-width: 12rem; font-weight: 600; background: none; }
table.summary th[scope=row] a { color: inherit; }
.status-line { font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 1rem; }
.status-line .chip { font-size: .9rem; margin-right: .4rem; }
table.review-box { max-width: 52rem; }
table.review-box th { width: 12rem; }
table.review-box td.write { height: 5rem; }
table.review-box td.write-line { height: 2.2rem; }
h2.first { border-top: 0; margin-top: 1.5rem; }
.chip { display: inline-block; font-size: .75rem; font-weight: 600; padding: .1rem .5rem; border-radius: 3px; white-space: nowrap; }
.s-PASS, .s-evaluated-PASS { background: var(--pass-bg); color: var(--pass); }
.chip.status-PASS { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info); } /* "No flags": neutral, not "passed" */
.s-WARN { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn); }
.s-FAIL { background: var(--fail-bg); color: var(--fail); }
.s-INFO, .s-none { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info); }
.s-INCOMPLETE { background: var(--incomplete-bg); color: var(--incomplete); }

table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .88rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: .45rem .65rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; }
thead th { background: #EAEFF3; font-weight: 600; }
tr.group th { background: #F1F4F7; font-size: .8rem; color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; }
td.num { font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; white-space: nowrap; }
.nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
details.more { display: inline; } details.more summary { cursor: pointer; color: var(--muted); display: inline; }
td.note { color: var(--muted); }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
.seq { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .92rem; letter-spacing: .04em; word-break: break-all; }
.seq .tail { font-weight: 700; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
pre { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .78rem; background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule);
  padding: .75rem 1rem; overflow-x: auto; line-height: 1.35; }
details { margin: .75rem 0; }
summary { cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: .9rem; }
summary:focus-visible, a:focus-visible { outline: 3px solid #3B5B7A; outline-offset: 2px; }
a[href^="https://www.ncbi"] { color: #2A5B8A; text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
figure { margin: 1rem 0; } figcaption { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted); font-family: var(--sans); }
.notice { background: var(--panel); border: 1px solid var(--rule); padding: .9rem 1.1rem; }
.notice p { margin: .35rem 0; }
footer { margin-top: 3rem; padding-top: 1rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--rule); }

@media print {
  html { background: #fff; } main { max-width: none; padding: 0; }
  table, pre, figure, .notice { break-inside: avoid; }
  h2 { break-after: avoid; } details:not([open]) > *:not(summary) { display: block; }
}
.s-critical, .s-likely_detected { background: var(--fail-bg); color: var(--fail); }
.s-warning, .s-amplified_not_detected { background: var(--warn-bg); color: var(--warn); }
.s-minor { background: var(--info-bg); color: var(--info); }
pre.aln { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: .78rem; line-height: 1.3; margin: .2rem 0 0; padding: 0; border: 0; background: none; overflow-x: auto; white-space: pre; }
.aln .mm { background: var(--fail-bg); color: var(--fail); font-weight: 700; }
.aln .gp { background: var(--warn-bg); }
.aln .un { color: var(--muted); }
.aln .tail { text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-thickness: 2px; text-underline-offset: 2px; }
td.aln-cell { white-space: nowrap; }
td.org { min-width: 16rem; }
svg.chart { width: 100%; max-width: 44rem; height: auto; display: block; }
details.qc > summary { cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--sans); color: var(--muted); margin: .4rem 0 1rem; }
details.changes { margin: 0; } details.changes > summary { cursor: pointer; list-style: none; font-size: .85rem; }
details.changes > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
pre.aln.compact { font-size: .92rem; letter-spacing: .04em; } /* as .seq: lines up with the header */
table.frag th .seq { white-space: nowrap; word-break: normal; }
div.channel + div.channel { margin-top: .35rem; }
table.frag td.types { min-width: 9rem; max-width: 15rem; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
{% macro chip(status) %}<span class="chip s-{{ status }} status-{{ status }}">{{ {'PASS': 'No flags', 'WARN': 'Review', 'FAIL': 'Exceeds limit', 'INCOMPLETE': 'Incomplete', 'INFO': 'Info'}.get(status, status) }}</span>{% endmacro %}
{% macro qc_chip(status) %}<span class="chip s-{{ status }}">{{ {'PASS': 'within', 'WARN': 'outside preferred', 'FAIL': 'outside limit', 'INFO': 'info'}.get(status, status) }}</span>{% endmacro %}
{% macro match(row, primer) %}{% if row.grade %}<span class="chip {{ grade_css(row.grade) }}" title="{{ row.grade_note }}">{{ row.grade | replace('_', ' ') }}</span><br>{% endif %}{% if row.note %}<strong>{{ row.note }}</strong><br>{% endif %}{% if row.n_mismatch == 0 and row.n_gap == 0 %}perfect match{% else %}{{ row.n_mismatch }} mismatch{{ 'es' if row.n_mismatch != 1 }}{% if row.n_gap %}, {{ row.n_gap }} gap{{ 's' if row.n_gap != 1 }}{% endif %}{% if primer %}<br><span class="meta">{% if row.clean_3prime_nt >= 5 %}3′ end intact ({{ row.clean_3prime_nt }} matching nt){% else %}<strong>mismatch in the 3′ end</strong> ({{ row.clean_3prime_nt }} matching nt){% endif %}</span>{% endif %}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro grade_css(g) %}{{ {'perfect': 's-PASS', 'tolerated': 's-PASS', 'at_risk': 's-WARN', 'likely_failure': 's-FAIL', 'indeterminate': 's-INCOMPLETE'}.get(g, 's-INFO') }}{% endmacro %}
{% macro pct(value) %}{% if 0 < value < 0.05 %}&lt;0.1%{% else %}{{ '%.1f' % value }}%{% endif %}{% endmacro %}

<header>
  <h1>{{ assay.assay_name }}</h1>
  <p class="meta">
    Assay evaluation record · generated {{ r.generated_at }} · qpcr-assay-check v{{ r.tool.version }} ·
    run <code>{{ r.run_id }}</code><br>
    Inputs hash (SHA-256): <code>{{ r.inputs_hash }}</code>
  </p>
</header>

<h2 id="summary" class="first">Summary of this year's check</h2>
<p>What was checked and what was found. The status marks where a limit you configured was crossed or evidence is missing; it is not a pass or fail of the assay. The laboratory decides what to do (reviewer's decision below).</p>
{% set flagged = summary | selectattr('css', 'in', ['WARN', 'FAIL']) | list %}
{% set missing = summary | selectattr('css', 'equalto', 'INCOMPLETE') | list %}
<p class="status-line"><span class="chip s-{{ r.overall.verdict.value }} status-{{ r.overall.verdict.value }}">{{ status_label }}</span>
  {{ flagged | length }} of {{ summary | length }} checks flagged for review{% if missing %}, {{ missing | length }} with evidence incomplete or not assessed{% endif %}.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table class="summary">
  <thead><tr><th>What was checked</th><th>Scope</th><th>Result</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for row in summary %}
  <tr><th scope="row">{% if row.anchor %}<a href="#{{ row.anchor }}">{{ row.check }}</a>{% else %}{{ row.check }}{% endif %}</th>
    <td class="note">{{ row.scope }}</td>
    <td>{{ row.result | ncbi }}</td>
    <td><span class="chip s-{{ row.css }} status-{{ row.css }}">{{ row.label }}</span>{% if row.reason %}<br><span class="meta">{{ row.reason | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">Status: <em>No flags</em>, no limit crossed; <em>Review</em>, a review (WARN) limit you configured was crossed; <em>Exceeds limit</em>, a FAIL limit was crossed; <em>Incomplete</em> or <em>Not assessed</em>, evidence is missing, which never counts as no flags. The limits are in the configuration (Methods). Every row is explained in its section below.</p>
{% if r.overall.rationale %}
<details class="findings"><summary>All findings behind this summary ({{ r.overall.rationale | length }})</summary>
<ul>{% for line in r.overall.rationale %}<li>{{ line | ncbi }}</li>{% endfor %}</ul>
</details>
{% endif %}

<h3>Reviewer's decision</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table class="review-box">
  <tbody>
  <tr><th scope="row">Decision</th><td>&#9744; No action &nbsp;&nbsp; &#9744; Monitor next year &nbsp;&nbsp; &#9744; Wet-lab check &nbsp;&nbsp; &#9744; Redesign</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Reason and actions</th><td class="write"></td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Name</th><td class="write-line"></td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Date and signature</th><td class="write-line"></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">For the laboratory's own record: filled in by the reviewer, on paper or in the quality system. The tool never fills it in.</p>

<p class="meta">{% if r.network_used %}This run sent the oligo sequences to NCBI (see Methods).{% else %}No sequence was searched against any database in this run, and no data was sent to NCBI.{% endif %}</p>

<h2>Assay as evaluated</h2>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tbody>
    {% set kinds = {'forward': 'Forward primer', 'reverse': 'Reverse primer', 'probe': 'Probe'} %}
    {% for o in assay.oligo_list %}
    <tr><th scope="row">{{ kinds[o.role] }}{% if o.name != o.role %} <span class="meta">{{ o.name }}</span>{% endif %}</th>
      <td>{{ o.sequence | seq_html(0 if o.role == 'probe' else 5) }} <span class="meta">{{ o.sequence | length }} nt</span>
      {% if o.role == 'probe' %}<br><span class="meta">reporter {{ o.reporter or 'not specified' }} / quencher {{ o.quencher or 'not specified' }}; modifications: {{ o.modifications | join(', ') or 'none declared' }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
    {% if assay.multi_oligo %}<tr><th scope="row">Reaction mix</th><td>Oligos of the same role are alternatives in the same mix: for each record the best-binding one counts. Probes with the same reporter are alternatives; probes with different reporters detect different regions.</td></tr>{% endif %}
    <tr><th scope="row">Template</th><td>{{ assay.template_type.value }}{% if assay.template_type.value == 'RNA' %} (reverse transcription step assumed){% endif %}</td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row">Intended target</th><td>
      {% if assay.target.taxid %}taxonomy ID {{ assay.target.taxid | taxon }}{% endif %}
      {% if assay.target.accession %}{% if assay.target.taxid %}; {% endif %}reference {{ assay.target.accession | ncbi }}{% endif %}
      {% if assay.target.gene %}; gene {{ assay.target.gene }}{% endif %}
      {% if assay.target.taxa %}<br><strong>Excluding</strong> these taxa and their descendants from the target (left out of the target search, inclusivity and the variant analysis; records of such organisms filed under another taxon, e.g. an unclassified one, stay in the target):
      {% set mnd = assay.target.taxa | selectattr('role', 'equalto', 'must_not_detect') | list %}{% set oos = assay.target.taxa | selectattr('role', 'equalto', 'out_of_scope') | list %}
      {% if mnd %}<br><em>Must not detect</em> ({{ mnd | length }}; searched as near neighbours, part of the specificity status): {% for x in mnd %}{{ x.taxid | taxon }}{% if x.reason %} ({{ x.reason }}){% endif %}{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}
      {% if oos %}<br><em>Out of scope</em> ({{ oos | length }}; searched and listed as "also detects", information only, not part of the status): {% for x in oos %}{{ x.taxid | taxon }}{% if x.reason %} ({{ x.reason }}){% endif %}{{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endif %}</td></tr>
    {% if assay.oligo_source %}<tr><th scope="row">Oligo source</th><td>{{ assay.oligo_source }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if evidence_rows %}<tr><th scope="row">Laboratory evidence</th><td>{% for e, n in evidence_rows %}{{ e.oligo }} <span class="seq">{{ e.variant }}</span>: <strong>{{ e.outcome | replace('_', ' ') }}</strong> <span class="meta">({{ e.note }}); {% if n %}applied to {{ n }} record{{ '' if n == 1 else 's' }} in this run{% else %}<strong>matched no site in this run</strong>: check the oligo name and the variant string{% endif %}</span>{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}<br><span class="meta">A laboratory result replaces the in silico class for sites with exactly this variant (rule LAB: detected = tolerated, not detected = likely failure).</span></td></tr>{% endif %}
    {% if assay.notes %}<tr><th scope="row">Notes</th><td>{{ assay.notes | ncbi }}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">The last five nucleotides of each primer, the 3′ end the polymerase extends, are underlined. The probe is not extended, so it has no underline.</p>
{% set degenerate = qc.oligos | selectattr('degenerate') | list %}
{% if degenerate %}
<p>Degenerate oligos were expanded and every variant was evaluated; the worst variant decides each status:
  {% for o in degenerate %}{{ o.role }} → {{ o.n_variants }} variants{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}.</p>
{% endif %}

{% if spec %}
<h2 id="specificity">Specificity</h2>
<p>{{ chip(spec.verdict_sites.value) }} off-target primer and probe sites &nbsp; {{ chip(spec.verdict_amplicons.value) }} predicted off-target products</p>
{% macro site_line(x) %}{% if x.query != x.role %}{{ x.query }} {% endif %}on {{ x.accession | ncbi }} ({{ x.organism or 'unknown organism' }}): {{ x.n_mismatch }} mismatch{{ 'es' if x.n_mismatch != 1 }}{% if x.n_gap %}, {{ x.n_gap }} gap{{ 's' if x.n_gap != 1 }}{% endif %}{% if x.role != 'probe' %}, {{ x.clean_3prime_nt }} clean 3′ nt{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
<div class="notice">
{% for t in spec_overview %}
<p><strong>{{ t.title }}</strong> <span class="meta">({{ t.tier }}, {{ t.n_taxa }} tax{{ 'on' if t.n_taxa == 1 else 'a' }})</span>:
  {% if t.products %}<strong>{{ t.products }} predicted product{{ '' if t.products == 1 else 's' }}</strong>{% if t.detected %}, {{ t.detected }} detectable by the probe{% endif %}{% else %}<strong>no predicted product</strong>{% endif %}{% if t.tier == 'out_of_scope' %}; information only{% endif %}.
  {% if t.tier != 'out_of_scope' %}{% if t.by_design and t.discriminating %}Discrimination rests on the {{ t.discriminating | join(' and ') }} primer{{ 's' if t.discriminating | length > 1 }}; the {{ t.by_design | join(' and ') }} bind{{ 's' if t.by_design | length == 1 }} this tier perfectly{% if 'probe' in t.by_design %} (a probe gives signal only inside a product){% endif %}.{% elif 'forward' in t.by_design and 'reverse' in t.by_design and not t.products %}<strong>Both primers have a perfect site in this tier</strong>, but never facing each other on one record within product distance, so no product is predicted; check those records (a partial record or fragment can hide the other site). {% endif %}
  {% for role in ['forward', 'reverse'] if t.closest[role] %}Closest {{ role }} site: {{ site_line(t.closest[role]) }}. {% endfor %}{% endif %}
  {% if t.incomplete %}<span class="meta">Not every relevant alignment was assessed for {{ t.incomplete | join(', ') }} (hit list full or cut at max_sites_per_query){% if t.discriminating and t.by_design and t.discriminating_complete %}; the {{ t.discriminating | join(' and ') }} primer{{ 's' if t.discriminating | length > 1 }} were assessed completely{% endif %}.</span>{% else %}<span class="meta">Every relevant alignment was assessed.</span>{% endif %}</p>
{% endfor %}
<p class="meta"><strong>Scope.</strong> {{ spec.scope }} This covers only what was searched and says nothing about organisms outside those tiers.</p>
</div>

<h3>All findings</h3>
<ul>
{% for f in spec.findings %}
  <li>{{ chip(f.severity) }} {{ f.message }}</li>
{% endfor %}
</ul>

<h3>Searches</h3>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Taxa (NCBI taxonomy ID)</th><th>Searches</th><th>Complete</th><th>RIDs</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for t in search_rows %}
  <tr><td>{{ t.tier }}</td><td>{{ t.taxids[:5] | map('taxon') | join(', ') }}{% if t.taxids | length > 5 %} <details class="more"><summary>+{{ t.taxids | length - 5 }} more</summary>{{ t.taxids[5:] | map('taxon') | join(', ') }}</details>{% endif %}{% if t.tier == 'target' and assay.target.excluded_taxids %} <details class="more"><summary>excluding {{ assay.target.excluded_taxids | length }} taxa</summary>{{ assay.target.excluded_taxids | map('taxon') | join(', ') }}</details>{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ t.n }}</td>
    <td>{% if t.tier == 'target' %}<span class="meta">not used for specificity{% if r.inclusivity and r.inclusivity.exhaustive %}; inclusivity and variants use every record of the target{% endif %}</span>{% elif t.saturated or (spec.counts | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', t.tier) | selectattr('truncated') | list) %}no: {{ ((t.saturated + (spec.counts | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', t.tier) | selectattr('truncated') | map(attribute='query') | list)) | unique | list) | join(', ') }}{% else %}yes{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{% for rid, day in t.rids %}{{ rid }}{% if day %} <span class="meta">{{ day }}</span>{% endif %}{% if not loop.last %}<br>{% endif %}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">Complete: every relevant alignment of every oligo was assessed (no full hit list, nothing cut at max_sites_per_query). RIDs are NCBI's search IDs, with the day they were issued; NCBI keeps results for about 36 hours, so they record provenance rather than live links.</p>
<details class="qc"><summary>Hits and alignments per oligo</summary>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Query</th><th>BLAST hits</th><th>Hit list full</th><th>Relevant alignments</th><th>Assessed</th><th>Cut by cap</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for t in search_rows %}{% for q, n in t.hits.items() %}{% set c = spec.counts | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', t.tier) | selectattr('query', 'equalto', q) | first %}
  <tr><td>{{ t.tier }}</td><td>{{ q }}</td><td class="num">{{ n }}</td><td>{{ 'yes' if q in t.saturated else 'no' }}</td>{% if c %}<td class="num">{{ c.hsps_relevant }}</td><td class="num">{{ c.sites_assessed }}</td><td>{{ 'yes' if c.truncated else 'no' }}</td>{% else %}<td colspan="3" class="meta">{{ 'not used for specificity' if t.tier == 'target' else '' }}</td>{% endif %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}{% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">Sites found: {{ spec.n_sites.critical }} critical, {{ spec.n_sites.warning }} warning, {{ spec.n_sites.minor }} minor.
  Levels follow the configured limits (mismatches, gaps and clean 3′ nucleotides). {{ spec.n_fetched }} sequence windows were used for full-length
  re-alignment{% if spec.n_fetch_failed %}; {{ spec.n_fetch_failed }} could not be fetched{% endif %}.</p>
</details>

<h2>Predicted off-target products</h2>
{% macro product_table(groups) %}<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Tier</th><th>Species</th><th>Products</th><th>Probe signal</th><th>Closest product</th><th>Length</th><th>Primer pairs</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for g in groups %}
  <tr><td>{{ g.tier }}</td><td>{{ g.species }}{% if g.names | length > 1 %}<br><span class="meta">{% for n, c in g.names.most_common(3) %}{{ n }} ({{ c }}){{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% if g.names | length > 3 %} and {{ g.names | length - 3 }} more{% endif %}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.n_products }}<br><span class="meta">{{ g.n_records }} record{{ '' if g.n_records == 1 else 's' }}</span></td>
    <td>{% if g.n_detected %}{{ chip('likely_detected') }} {{ g.n_detected }}{% if assay.channels | length > 1 and g.channels %}<br><span class="meta">{% for ch, c in g.channels.most_common() %}{{ ch }} ({{ c }}){{ ', ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</span>{% endif %}{% endif %}{% if g.n_products - g.n_detected %}{% if g.n_detected %}<br>{% endif %}{{ chip('amplified_not_detected') }} {{ g.n_products - g.n_detected }}{% endif %}</td>
    <td>{{ g.best_mismatches }} primer mismatch{{ '' if g.best_mismatches == 1 else 'es' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ g.best.accession | ncbi }} {{ g.best.start }}–{{ g.best.end }}</span></td>
    <td class="num">{{ g.length_range }}</td><td>{% for pair, c in g.pairs.most_common(3) %}{{ pair }}{% if g.pairs | length > 1 %} ({{ c }}){% endif %}{{ '<br>' | safe if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>{% endmacro %}
{% if spec.amplicons %}
{% set judged = product_groups | rejectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'out_of_scope') | list %}
{% set oos = product_groups | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'out_of_scope') | list %}
<p class="meta">One row per search tier and species (identical products counted once), most concerning first: products the probe would detect, then the fewest primer mismatches. Every product is listed in the workbook (sheet "Predicted products"). A product is predicted when two primer sites of at least warning level face each other on the same record within {{ r.config.specificity.max_amplicon_size }} bp; {{ spec.n_primer_only }} primer site(s) at warning or critical level formed no product.</p>
{% if judged %}{{ product_table(products_shown[0]) }}{% if products_shown[1] %}<p class="meta">{{ products_shown[1] }} further species row(s) with products the probe would not detect: see the workbook.</p>{% endif %}
{% else %}<p>No product was predicted in the judged tiers ({{ spec.counts | map(attribute='tier') | reject('equalto', 'out_of_scope') | unique | join(', ') or 'none searched' }}).</p>{% endif %}
{% if assay.target.must_not_detect_taxids and not (judged | selectattr('tier', 'equalto', 'near_neighbours') | list) %}<p><strong>No product predicted in the taxa the assay must not detect</strong> ({{ assay.target.must_not_detect_taxids | length }} taxa, searched as near neighbours).</p>{% endif %}
{% if oos %}<details><summary><strong>Also detects (out of scope, information only):</strong> {{ oos | sum(attribute='n_products') }} product(s) in {{ oos | length }} species</summary>
<p class="meta">Taxa the assay is allowed to detect but that are not its intended target (<code>target.taxa</code> with role out_of_scope); not part of the specificity status.</p>
{{ product_table(oos) }}</details>{% endif %}
{% else %}
<p>No product was predicted from primer sites of at least warning level in the searched tiers.</p>
{% if assay.target.must_not_detect_taxids %}<p><strong>No product predicted in the taxa the assay must not detect</strong> ({{ assay.target.must_not_detect_taxids | length }} taxa, searched as near neighbours).</p>{% endif %}
{% endif %}

{% if r.variant_summary and ((r.variant_summary.oligos | selectattr('rows') | list) or r.variant_summary.coverage) %}
<h2 id="variants">Variant summary (assay's own target)</h2>
{% set cov = r.variant_summary.coverage %}
{% if cov %}
{% if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' %}<div class="notice"><p><strong>Scope: every NCBI Nucleotide record{% if not cov.complete %} assessed so far{% endif %}.</strong> Built from the Nucleotide records of the target (taxonomy ID {{ cov.taxon }}{% if cov.filters.excluded_taxids %}, excluding {{ cov.filters.excluded_taxids }}{% endif %}){% if cov.filters.nucleotide_query %}, narrowed by <code>{{ cov.filters.nucleotide_query }}</code>{% endif %}, newest publication year first. The {{ cov.amplicon_length }} bp reference amplicon ({{ cov.amplicon_source }}) was BLASTed against lists of at most {{ r.config.variants.blast_records_per_search }} of these records at a time, so no search could fill its hit list; hits outside each list were ignored, and partial hits were completed from the record itself. These are counts over all assessed records, not a sample. A record without the region is usually a different gene or a partial sequence, not a missing target.</p></div>
{% else %}<div class="notice"><p><strong>Scope: every genome assembly{% if not cov.complete %} assessed so far{% endif %}.</strong> Built from the genome assemblies of the target (taxonomy ID {{ cov.taxon }}) in NCBI Datasets: current versions{% if cov.filters.exclude_atypical %}, atypical assemblies excluded{% endif %}, one copy per GenBank/RefSeq pair. Each genome was scanned for the {{ cov.amplicon_length }} bp reference amplicon ({{ cov.amplicon_source }}); the oligos were re-aligned end to end in the best complete copy. These are counts over all assessed assemblies, not a sample. Sequences submitted without a genome assembly (single genes, amplicons) are not part of this collection.</p></div>{% endif %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <tbody>
  <tr><th scope="row">{{ 'Records' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'Assemblies' }} listed</th><td>{{ cov.listed_total }} (listed {{ cov.listed_at }})</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Assessed</th><td>{{ cov.assessed_total }}{% if not cov.complete %} &mdash; <strong>incomplete</strong>: at most {{ cov.budget_per_run }} new {{ 'records' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'assemblies' }} are processed per run, newest first; run again to continue{% endif %}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Processed in this run</th><td>{{ cov.processed_this_run }}{% if cov.download_failed_this_run %}; {{ cov.download_failed_this_run }} download(s) failed and will be retried next run{% endif %}{% if cov.unavailable %}<br><span class="meta">{{ cov.unavailable }} could not be downloaded after repeated attempts; they are left out, not counted as work still to do, and tried again on each run: {{ cov.unavailable_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Amplicon region found</th><td>{{ cov.found }} with all three oligo sites complete</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Region cut by a {{ 'record' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'contig' }} end</th><td>{{ cov.contig_break }} ({{ 'the record ends inside the amplicon' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'draft assemblies' }}; not counted in the tables)</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Region hidden by N</th><td>{{ cov.masked }}{% if cov.masked_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cov.masked_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}<br><span class="meta">The region is there, but the whole region or an oligo site in it reads N (low-coverage sequencing): not counted in the tables, since an N is neither a match nor a variant. A region that is N from end to end is placed by the reference sequence on either side of the amplicon (from the assay's target accession).</span></td></tr>
  {% if cov.related_only %}<tr><th scope="row">Related regions, not the target</th><td><strong>{{ cov.related_only }}</strong> {{ 'record(s)' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'genome(s)' }} in which the only regions found resemble the target but do not meet the copy rule (at least {{ r.config.variants.min_anchored_bases | default(32) }} fragment bases in exact blocks, or {{ r.config.variants.min_context_bases | default(32) }} anchored bases of the sequence either side, or {{ '%g' % (100 * cov.min_copy_identity) }}% identity with {{ r.config.variants.min_identity_anchored_bases | default(16) }} anchored bases): not a copy of the target, not in the tables{% if cov.related_only_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cov.related_only_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}<br><span class="meta">A region is found through exact {{ r.config.variants.seed_length }}-base stretches of the fragment; a single chance stretch can point to an unrelated region (measured: at most 18 anchored bases by chance). Settings variants.min_anchored_bases, min_context_bases, min_copy_identity, min_identity_anchored_bases.</span></td></tr>{% endif %}
  <tr><th scope="row">Region not found</th><td>{{ cov.not_found }}{% if cov.not_found_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cov.not_found_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}<br><span class="meta">No exact {{ r.config.variants.seed_length }}-base stretch of the amplicon anywhere in the {{ 'record' if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' else 'genome' }}: the target region may be absent, or too divergent to find. Where the reference sequence around the amplicon was found, the region there reads real bases, not N; without a target accession in the assay, a region wholly hidden by N is also counted here.</span>
    {% if not cov.target_on_plasmid %}<br>of which {{ cov.not_found_without_plasmid }} contain no sequence labelled as a plasmid and {{ cov.not_found_with_plasmid }} contain plasmid sequence{% if cov.target_on_plasmid is none %} (whether the target lies on a plasmid is not known yet){% endif %}.{% endif %}
    {% if cov.target_on_plasmid %}<br>of which <strong>{{ cov.not_found_without_plasmid }}</strong> contain no sequence labelled as a plasmid (many assemblies hold only the chromosome, which says nothing about the strain; in a draft assembly a plasmid can also sit in an unlabelled contig, so a deletion there would be counted here), and <strong>{{ cov.not_found_with_plasmid }}</strong> contain a sequence labelled as a plasmid but not the target region{% if cov.not_found_with_plasmid %} &mdash; <strong>review these</strong>: a possible deletion the assay would miss (as with the Swedish nvCT variant), or an incomplete plasmid assembly: {{ cov.not_found_with_plasmid_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}{% endif %}.{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% if cov.target_on_plasmid is not none %}<tr><th scope="row">Target on a plasmid</th><td>{{ 'yes' if cov.target_on_plasmid else 'no' }} (where the region was found, it lies on a sequence whose description {{ 'names' if cov.target_on_plasmid else 'does not name' }} a plasmid){% if cov.plasmid_header_examples %}<br><span class="meta">Recognised as plasmid, e.g.: {{ cov.plasmid_header_examples[:3] | join('; ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  {% if cov.source == 'blast_partitioned' %}<tr><th scope="row">How records were checked</th><td>{{ cov.found_by_direct_scan }} with the region found by fetching and scanning the record itself (records up to {{ r.config.variants.direct_scan_max_length }} bases); longer records by BLAST in accession lists{% if cov.not_checked_directly %}<br><strong>{{ cov.not_checked_directly }}</strong> longer record(s) had no BLAST hit and were not scanned directly: their "not found" rests on BLAST alone{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
  <tr><th scope="row">More than one copy</th><td>{{ cov.multi_copy }} (each genome is judged by the copy the assay binds best; see below)</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% set cc = cov.copies %}
{% set judged_n = (cc.genomes - (0 if cc.from_parts_counted else cc.from_parts)) if cc else 0 %}
{% if cc and cc.genomes %}
<h3>Copies, coverage per oligo, and escapes</h3>
<p class="meta">Every stored copy of the region is assessed with every oligo of the mix. A site is <em>detectable</em> when its graded mismatch class is <em>perfect</em> or <em>tolerated</em> (see "Mismatch classes" under Inclusivity; primers: Stadhouders 2010 and Lefever 2013; probes: at most 1 mismatch outside the last 5 nucleotides, and none for MGB probes){% if cc.homopolymer_bulges_detectable %}, or with no mismatch and only a gap from a single-base run of another length (a homopolymer bulge, e.g. poly-A 7&rarr;8; setting <code>variants.homopolymer_bulges_detectable: true</code>){% else %}; a primer site that differs only by the length of a single-base run (a homopolymer bulge, e.g. poly-A 7&rarr;8) is <em>at risk</em> when one base differs and the run stays out of the last 3 nucleotides, otherwise <em>likely failure</em> (rule R5b; no PCR study measured such bulges), and not counted as detectable (setting <code>variants.homopolymer_bulges_detectable: false</code>){% endif %}; a copy is detectable when every role is; each genome is judged by its best copy, as the PCR needs only one copy it can amplify. The variant tables below use that best copy.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table><tbody>
  <tr><th scope="row">Genomes assessed</th><td>{{ cc.genomes }}; {{ cc.multi_copy }} with more than one copy (at most {{ cc.max_copies }})</td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">Best copy not the first found</th><td>{{ cc.best_copy_not_first }}<br><span class="meta">genomes whose best-binding copy differs from the copy found most confidently (earlier versions assessed only that one)</span></td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row">With a detectable copy</th><td>{{ cc.with_detectable_copy }} of {{ cc.genomes }} ({{ pct(100.0 * cc.with_detectable_copy / cc.genomes) }}; homopolymer bulges {{ 'counted as detectable' if cc.homopolymer_bulges_detectable else 'not counted (strict)' }})<br><span class="meta">Under both rules: {{ cc.with_detectable_copy_strict }} ({{ pct(100.0 * cc.with_detectable_copy_strict / cc.genomes) }}) strict; {{ cc.with_detectable_copy_bulges }} ({{ pct(100.0 * cc.with_detectable_copy_bulges / cc.genomes) }}) if homopolymer bulges are tolerated. Whether a bulge is amplified or detected is not known from sequence alone; a wet-lab check decides.</span></td></tr>
  <tr><th scope="row"><strong>Escapes</strong></th><td><strong>{{ cc.escapes }}</strong> genome(s) without a detectable copy{% if cc.escape_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cc.escape_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% if cc.run_length %}{% set rl = cc.run_length %}<tr><th scope="row">Homopolymer length variants</th><td>{{ rl.genomes }} genome(s) with a site that differs from an oligo only by the length of a single-base run in at least one copy; {{ rl.on_best_copy }} are judged on such a copy, and the detection of {{ rl.decided_by_rule }} depends on the homopolymer-bulge setting (see above).
  <br><span class="meta">Run length is a known sequencing and assembly error, so check how far to trust these: in {{ rl.mixed }} of the {{ rl.genomes }} genomes the copies disagree (other copies read the oligo's run length at that site), which is either real copy variation or an error in some copies. By assembly level (genomes with a variant / assessed): {% for level, (n, tot) in rl.by_level.items() %}{{ level }} {{ n }}/{{ tot }} ({{ pct(100.0 * n / tot) if tot else '–' }}){{ '; ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}. Far more variants in draft than in complete genomes points to assembly error. Most frequent: {% for v, n in rl.variants %}{{ v }} ({{ n }}){{ '; ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.</span></td></tr>{% endif %}
{% if cc.undetermined %}<tr><th scope="row">Undetermined</th><td>{{ cc.undetermined }} genome(s) without a detectable copy whose only problem has no published basis: a single mismatch in an MGB probe, or an ambiguity code in the genome near a 3′ end that decides whether the site is detectable. Counted neither as detected nor as an escape; a wet-lab check decides.{% if cc.undetermined_examples %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cc.undetermined_examples[:10] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>{% endif %}
{% if cc.from_parts %}<tr><th scope="row">Detectable from parts</th><td><strong>{{ cc.from_parts }}</strong> genome(s) whose copies of the region are cut by a contig end (or whose best whole copy fails), but that carry a detectable site of every role, each whole on a cut copy (repeats such as rRNA operons break draft assemblies). The sites may come from different copies, so this is not proof of one amplifiable fragment; {% if cc.from_parts_counted %}counted as detected{% else %}counted as undetermined, neither detected nor an escape, and left out of the per-oligo and channel counts{% endif %} (setting variants.judge_from_parts). Listed in the workbook (sheet "From parts").</td></tr>{% endif %}
{% if cc.unassembled %}<tr><th scope="row">Copies possibly unassembled</th><td><strong>{{ cc.unassembled }}</strong> draft genome(s) whose best copy fails but that carry fewer than half the copies of the complete and chromosome-level genomes of this run (median {{ '%g' % cc.typical_copies }} copies), with more than one sequence or a copy cut by a contig end. Near-identical repeat copies are often left unassembled in drafts (as N gaps or collapsed into one), so the copy judged may not be the one the PCR would amplify. Counted as undetermined, neither detected nor as an escape, unless a complete or chromosome-level genome fails with the same three sites. This can hide a real loss of copies: check the list in the workbook (sheet "Unassembled"). Setting variants.multicopy_unassembled.</td></tr>{% endif %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% if cc.by_level %}
<h4>Detection by assembly level</h4>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Assembly level</th><th>Genomes</th><th>Detectable</th><th>Escapes</th><th>Undetermined</th>{% if cc.unassembled %}<th>Possibly unassembled</th>{% endif %}{% if cc.from_parts and not cc.from_parts_counted %}<th>Detectable from parts</th>{% endif %}</tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for lv in cc.by_level %}
  <tr><td>{{ lv.level }}</td><td class="num">{{ lv.genomes }}</td><td class="num">{{ lv.detectable }}{% if lv.percent is not none %} <span class="meta">({{ pct(lv.percent) }})</span>{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ lv.escapes }}</td><td class="num">{{ lv.undetermined }}</td>{% if cc.unassembled %}<td class="num">{{ lv.unassembled }}</td>{% endif %}{% if cc.from_parts and not cc.from_parts_counted %}<td class="num">{{ lv.from_parts }}</td>{% endif %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
<p class="meta">Percentages leave the undetermined (and possibly unassembled) genomes out. Complete genomes are a small subset that is not representative (reference strains, recent long-read sequencing), so they are no substitute for the overall figure. But draft assemblies (Scaffold, Contig) can leave near-identical repeat copies unassembled, as N gaps or cut at contig ends: for a multi-copy target, escapes that occur far more often in drafts than in complete genomes point to the assembly rather than to the strain. The "Needs attention" rows give the assembly levels of their genomes under the types.</p>
{% endif %}
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Role</th><th>Oligo</th><th>Covers (best copy)</th><th>Only this oligo</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for role in ['forward', 'reverse', 'probe'] %}
  {% for o in cc.oligos if o.role == role %}
  <tr><td>{{ role }}</td><td>{{ o.name }}{% if o.reporter %} <span class="meta">{{ o.reporter }}</span>{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ o.covered }} ({{ pct(100.0 * o.covered / judged_n) if judged_n else '–' }})</td><td class="num">{% if assay.by_role(role) | length > 1 %}{{ o.only }}{% else %}–{% endif %}</td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  {% if cc.role_undetermined.get(role) %}<tr><td>{{ role }}</td><td><em>undetermined</em></td><td class="num">{{ cc.role_undetermined[role] }}</td><td></td></tr>{% endif %}
  <tr><td>{{ role }}</td><td><em>none of them</em></td><td class="num"><strong>{{ cc.role_none[role] }}</strong>{% if cc.role_none_examples[role] %}<br><span class="meta">e.g. {{ cc.role_none_examples[role][:5] | join(', ') | ncbi }}</span>{% endif %}</td><td></td></tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if cc.channels | length > 1 and not channel_table %}
<p><strong>Probe channels</strong> (probes with different reporters detect different regions; counted as detected when <strong>{{ 'any channel' if cc.probe_channels == 'any' else 'every channel' }}</strong> detects, setting <code>variants.probe_channels</code>):</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Reporter</th><th>Probes</th><th>Genomes detected</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% for ch in cc.channels %}<tr><td>{{ ch.reporter }}</td><td>{{ ch.probes | join(', ') }}</td><td class="num">{{ ch.covered }}</td></tr>{% endfor %}
  <tr><td colspan="2">any channel</td><td class="num">{{ cc.any_channel }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td colspan="2">all channels</td><td class="num">{{ cc.all_channels }}</td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% endif %}
{% endif %}
{% else %}
<div class="notice"><p><strong>Scope.</strong> Built from the target tier's own BLAST hits: at most {{ r.config.search.hitlist_size }} per oligo, the closest site per record, with partial hits fetched and re-aligned across the whole oligo. Identical alignments are lumped together and each is reported as a percentage of that measured total. When the hit list is full (see Searches) this is BLAST's selection of records, not the whole target population and not a random sample; see Inclusivity below for the year-by-year view against population counts.</p></div>
{% endif %}

<h3>Whole fragment (forward + probe + reverse combined)</h3>
{% macro oligo_no(role, name) %}{% set olis = assay.by_role(role) %}{% if olis | length > 1 %}{% for o in olis %}{% if o.name == name %}({{ loop.index }}){% endif %}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro role_head(title, role) %}{% set olis = assay.by_role(role) %}<th>{{ title }}{% for o in olis %}<br><span class="meta"><span class="seq" title="{{ o.name }}">{{ o.sequence }}</span>{% if olis | length > 1 %} ({{ loop.index }}){% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}</th>{% endmacro %}
{% if fragments %}
{% set fv = fragments %}
{% macro outcome_chip(o) %}<span class="chip {{ {'detectable': 's-PASS', 'at risk': 's-WARN', 'likely failure': 's-FAIL', 'undetermined': 's-INCOMPLETE'}.get(o, 's-INFO') }}">{{ o or 'not classified' }}</span>{% endmacro %}
{% macro site_inner(v, role, tail=5) %}{% if v.grade %}<span class="chip {{ grade_css(v.grade) }}" title="{{ v.grade_note }}">{{ v.grade | replace('_', ' ') }}</span>{% endif %}{% set freq = site_pct.get((role, v.q_aln, v.s_aln)) %}{% if freq is not none and v.grade != 'perfect' %} <span class="meta" title="this {{ role }} site variant, whatever the other sites are">{{ pct(freq) }}</span>{% endif %}<span title="{{ v.oligo_name }}: {{ v.n_mismatch }} mismatch(es), {{ v.n_gap }} gap(s){% if v.note %}; {{ v.note }}{% endif %}">{{ v | aln_compact(tail, oligo_no(role, v.oligo_name) | trim) }}</span>{% endmacro %}
{% macro site_cell(v, role, tail=5) %}<td class="aln-cell">{{ site_inner(v, role, tail) }}</td>{% endmacro %}
{% macro probe_cell(f) %}{% if f.channels %}<td class="aln-cell">{% for rep, v in f.channels %}<div class="channel"><span class="meta">{{ rep }}</span> {{ site_inner(v, 'probe', 0) }}</div>{% endfor %}</td>{% else %}{{ site_cell(f.probe, 'probe', 0) }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro types(orgs, total) %}{% for name, n in orgs[:3] %}{{ name }} {{ n }}{{ '; ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}{% if orgs | length > 3 %}; +{{ orgs | length - 3 }}{% endif %}{% endmacro %}
{% macro frag_rows(rows) %}{% for f, outcome, by_pair in rows %}
  <tr><td>{{ outcome_chip(outcome) }}{% if by_pair %}<br><span class="meta">primer-pair rule (Lefever 2013)</span>{% endif %}</td>
    {{ site_cell(f.forward, 'forward') }}{{ probe_cell(f) }}{{ site_cell(f.reverse, 'reverse') }}
    <td class="num">{{ f.count }}<br><span class="meta">{{ pct(f.percent) }}</span>{% if f.unassembled and outcome != 'detectable' %}<br><span class="meta" title="draft genomes with far fewer copies than the complete genomes: counted as undetermined">{{ f.unassembled }} possibly unassembled</span>{% endif %}{% if f.from_parts %}<br><span class="meta" title="every site found whole on copies cut by a contig end, possibly on different copies">{{ f.from_parts }} detectable from parts{% if not f.from_parts_counted %} (undetermined){% endif %}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    <td class="types">{{ types(f.organisms, f.count) }}{% if f.levels %}<br><span class="meta">{% for name, n in f.levels %}{{ name }} {{ n }}{{ '; ' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}</span>{% endif %}</td>
    {% if cov %}<td>{{ f.forward.first_seen or '' }}<br><span class="meta">{{ f.forward.last_seen or '' }}</span></td>{% endif %}
    <td>{{ f.example_accession | ncbi }}</td></tr>
{% endfor %}{% endmacro %}
{% set head %}<thead><tr><th>Outcome</th>{{ role_head('Forward', 'forward') }}{{ role_head('Probe', 'probe') }}{{ role_head('Reverse', 'reverse') }}<th>Records</th><th>Types</th>{% if cov %}<th>First / last release</th>{% endif %}<th>Example</th></tr></thead>{% endset %}
<p><strong>{{ fv.total }} records with all three sites:</strong>{% for o in ['detectable', 'at risk', 'likely failure', 'undetermined'] + (['possibly unassembled'] if fv.records.get('possibly unassembled') else []) + (['detectable from parts'] if fv.records.get('detectable from parts') else []) + (['not classified'] if fv.records.get('not classified') else []) %} {{ o }} {{ pct(100.0 * fv.records.get(o, 0) / fv.total) }}{{ ',' if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}.</p>
<p class="meta">Only this table shows which site variants occur <em>together</em> on one template, and so the outcome for the genome: the worst class of its three sites, and the primer-pair rule (3 + &ge;2 or 4 + 1 mismatches across the two primers). Each site is one line against the oligo in the column header: a dot is a matching base, a letter a mismatch (highlighted), '-' a gap; the primer 3′ end (last 5 nt) is underlined. {% for role in ['forward', 'probe', 'reverse'] %}{% set olis = assay.by_role(role) %}{% if olis | length > 1 %}{{ role | capitalize }}: {% for o in olis %}({{ loop.index }}) {{ o.name }}{{ ', ' if not loop.last else '. ' }}{% endfor %}{% endif %}{% endfor %}Next to the class of a site that is not perfect: how often that site variant occurs among all records of the oligo, whatever the other two sites are (see Variants per oligo). Types are the organism names of the records, and for genome assemblies their assembly levels (see "Detection by assembly level"). Classes present published primer-mismatch data (Stadhouders 2010, Lefever 2013), not predicted Cq values; in silico analysis does not replace experimental validation.</p>
{% set n_att = fv.attention | length + (fv.attention_grouped | sum(attribute=2)) %}<h4>Needs attention ({{ n_att }} combination{{ '' if n_att == 1 else 's' }})</h4>
{% if fv.attention %}
<div class="scroll"><table class="frag">{{ head }}<tbody>
{{ frag_rows(fv.attention) }}
{% for o, kinds, n, c, n_kinds in fv.attention_grouped %}
  <tr class="group"><td>{{ outcome_chip(o) }}</td><td colspan="{{ 7 if cov else 6 }}">{{ n }} further, less frequent combination(s): {{ c }} records ({{ pct(100.0 * c / fv.total) }}); types {{ types(kinds, 0) }}{% if n_kinds > 3 %} and {{ n_kinds - 3 }} more{% endif %}. Listed individually in the workbook (sheet "Fragment variants").</td></tr>
{% endfor %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% else %}<p>None: every combination is detectable.</p>{% endif %}
{% set n_det = fv.detectable_top | length + fv.detectable_rest %}<h4>Detectable ({{ n_det }} combination{{ '' if n_det == 1 else 's' }})</h4>
<div class="scroll"><table class="frag">{{ head }}<tbody>
{{ frag_rows(fv.detectable_top) }}
{% if fv.detectable_rest %}
  <tr class="group"><td>{{ outcome_chip('detectable') }}</td><td colspan="{{ 7 if cov else 6 }}"><strong>{{ fv.detectable_rest }} other detectable combination(s)</strong>, all sites perfect or tolerated: {{ fv.detectable_rest_records }} records ({{ pct(100.0 * fv.detectable_rest_records / fv.total) }}); types {{ types(fv.detectable_rest_types, 0) }}. All combinations are in the workbook (sheet "Fragment variants").</td></tr>
{% endif %}
</tbody></table></div>
{% else %}
<p>No target-tier record had all three sites (forward, probe, reverse) fully re-aligned, so no whole-fragment variant table could be built.</p>
{% endif %}
