{% if r.inclusivity.fragment_years %}
<h3>Whole fragment (forward + probe + reverse combined)</h3>
<p class="meta">The summary and the inclusivity status use this outcome, pooled over the last {{ r.config.inclusivity.verdict_window_years | default(3) }} complete release years and the current one (see Rationale below); when the pooled figure has no flags, a single year in that window with at least {{ r.config.inclusivity.min_genomes_per_year | default(30) }} genomes below the FAIL limit gives Review; smaller years are marked "few records" and only shown. Per year, each genome's outcome from its three sites together, as in the whole-fragment table: detectable when all three are perfect or tolerated, otherwise the worst site, and likely failure by the primer-pair rule (3 + &ge;2 or 4 + 1 mismatches across the two primers). Percentages are of the records with all three sites minus the undetermined ones, the same base as the summary; undetermined records are counted but not in a percentage. Years in the summary window are marked. The tables per oligo below show each site on its own; they explain the status but do not decide it.</p>
<div class="scroll"><table>
  <thead><tr><th>Year</th><th>{{ 'Records' if nuc else 'Assemblies' }}</th><th>With region</th><th>Detectable</th><th>At risk</th><th>Likely failure</th><th>Undetermined</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
  {% set fy = r.inclusivity.fragment_years %}
  {% set min_year = r.config.inclusivity.min_genomes_per_year | default(30) %}
  {% set last_year = (fy | selectattr('with_region') | map(attribute='year') | list or fy | map(attribute='year') | list) | max %}
  {% set first_window = last_year - (r.config.inclusivity.verdict_window_years | default(3)) %}
  {% macro frag_cells(det, risk, fail, undet, region, pair=0, unasm=0, parts=0) %}{% set base = region - undet %}{% for n in [det, risk, fail] %}<td class="num">{{ n }}{% if base > 0 %} <span class="meta">({{ pct(100.0 * n / base) }})</span>{% endif %}{% if loop.index == 3 and pair %}<br><span class="meta">{{ pair }} by the pair rule</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endfor %}<td class="num">{{ undet }}{% if unasm %}<br><span class="meta">{{ unasm }} possibly unassembled</span>{% endif %}{% if parts %}<br><span class="meta">{{ parts }} detectable from parts</span>{% endif %}</td>{% endmacro %}
  {% for f in fy %}
  <tr><td class="num">{{ f.year }}{% if f.year >= first_window %}<br><span class="meta">summary window</span>{% endif %}{% if f.with_region - f.undetermined < min_year %}<br><span class="meta">few records</span>{% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ f.population_size if f.population_size is not none else '–' }}</td><td class="num">{{ f.with_region }}</td>
