  <tr><td class="num">{{ w.year }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.population_size if w.population_size is not none else '–' }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ w.sample_size }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_perfect }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_one_mismatch }}</td>
    <td class="num">{{ w.n_two_plus_mismatch }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_three_prime_mismatch }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_fetch_failed }}</td>{% if w.n_detectable is not none %}<td class="num">{{ w.n_detectable }}{% if w.sample_size %} ({{ pct(100.0 * w.n_detectable / w.sample_size) }}){% endif %}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_by_grade.get('at_risk', 0) }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_by_grade.get('likely_failure', 0) }}</td><td class="num">{{ w.n_by_grade.get('indeterminate', 0) }}</td>{% elif o.windows | rejectattr('n_detectable', 'none') | list %}<td></td><td></td><td></td><td></td>{% endif %}</tr>
  {% endfor %}
  </tbody>
</table></div>
{% if loop.last and r.inclusivity.oligos | map(attribute='windows') | map('rejectattr', 'n_detectable', 'none') | map('list') | select | list %}
<h3>Mismatch classes</h3>
<p class="meta">Each oligo site on the target gets a class (docs/MISMATCH_CLASSES.md): <em>perfect</em>; <em>tolerated</em> (expected to cost little); <em>at risk</em> (a measurable delay is expected, worse near the limit of detection); <em>likely failure</em> (blocked or strongly delayed in the published data); <em>indeterminate</em> (no published basis: gaps together with mismatches that alone would not decide, ambiguity codes in the genome, a single mismatch in an MGB probe). <em>Detectable</em> = perfect or tolerated; the inclusivity limits apply to it. A single mismatch in an MGB probe and an ambiguity code in the genome near a 3′ end are <em>undetermined</em>: left out of the percentage (neither detected nor escaped). Gaps count as not detected. A primer site that differs only in the length of a single-base run (homopolymer bulge) is at risk for one base with the run outside the last 3 nt, otherwise likely failure (rule R5b; no PCR study measured such bulges; setting variants.homopolymer_bulges_detectable). Primers: single mismatches in the last 5 nt by type and position after Stadhouders et al., J Mol Diagn 2010 (Table 1, Taq polymerase on DNA); farther positions and the number of mismatches per primer and per primer pair after Lefever et al., Clin Chem 2013. Probes: no published rule was used; a probe without MGB tolerates 1 mismatch outside the last 5 nt; an MGB probe with 1 mismatch is undetermined and with 2 or more a likely failure. {{ grade_caveat }}</p>
{% endif %}
{% endfor %}
